laprdus (2.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Laprdus 2.0.
  * New voices synthesized by rule, clear at any rate: Zvonko (the default
    voice), Stojan and Mirsad; Bosnian is now supported, also under Speech
    Dispatcher.
  * Every voice speaks every language: Croatian, Serbian, Bosnian and
    Slovenian are chosen apart from the voice (CLI -L / --language; Speech
    Dispatcher SET LANGUAGE keeps the voice and lists every voice for every
    language). Slovenian is new: Pravopis pronunciation, a 25,000-word
    stress lexicon from Sloleks, Slovenian numbers, dates and letter names.
  * Word stress and natural sentence melody for every voice. Josip and Vlado
    have a new engine: no clicks, natural tempo, rate and pitch independent.
  * Ten singing voices (orguljas, dalmacija_klapa, lika_velebit, becarac,
    trubac, harmonikas, solunac, sevdalija, sazlija, sarajevo_bembasa).
  * Voice ids are plain ASCII (djedo for Đedo); the old ids djed, klapa,
    pjevac, pevac and solist are still accepted.
  * CLI options -I (inflection level) and -a (acceleration) for the new
    voices; Speech Dispatcher maps its pitch range onto the inflection level.
  * User accent dictionary accents.json next to the other user dictionaries.
  * Fixed: user spelling and emoji dictionaries had no effect; the derived
    voices detence, baba and djedo sounded like their base voice.
  * Library SONAME bumped to liblaprdus.so.2.

 -- Hrvoje Katic <hrvoje.katic@gmail.com>  Wed, 07 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200

laprdus (1.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release.
  * Croatian and Serbian text-to-speech synthesis
  * Speech Dispatcher integration for Orca screen reader
  * Command-line utility
  * Five voices: Josip, Vlado, Detence, Baba, Djedo

